---
import { imageUrl, latestPresentation } from '../../../site/src/lib/pingstore';
interface Props { experiment: string; }
const { experiment } = Astro.props;
const run = (await latestPresentation(experiment)).id;
---
<figure class="l-body" id="figure-2">
  <theta-ping-circuit data-source={await imageUrl(run, 'circuit.json')} data-condition="theta">
    <div class="scene" role="img" aria-label="Recorded circuit activity on the left and four synchronized pistons showing mean conductances onto E and mean E and I population voltages on the right, with the full afferent-rate protocol and a moving current-time bar below.">
      <p class="status" role="status">Loading recorded circuit…</p>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <label>Input <select data-condition aria-label="Afferent input condition"><option value="theta">Theta · 5 Hz · 0.2–3.8 Hz</option><option value="constant">Constant · 2 Hz</option></select></label>
      <input class="scrubber" type="range" data-scrub aria-label="Replay time" min="0" max="1000" step="0.1" value="0" disabled />
      <label class="speed-control">Speed <input type="range" data-speed min="0.25" max="4" step="0.25" value="1" disabled /><output data-speed-value>1×</output></label>
      <button type="button" data-pause disabled>Pause</button>
    </div>
    <noscript>This replay requires JavaScript. The recorded spike raster is available in Figure 3.</noscript>
  </theta-ping-circuit>
  <figcaption>Figure 2: Select the 5 Hz theta-modulated or constant-input recording. Each replays the complete one-second simulation from initialization, with no burn-in. A: Private inputs and population spikes are shown for 160 E-targeted and 40 I-targeted channels and their receiving neurons. Each channel aggregates 400 independent excitatory afferents. Blue denotes E-targeted channels and E neurons; rose denotes I-targeted channels and I neurons. Both private inputs are excitatory. Displayed recurrent edges exist in the simulated circuit. Pulses travel over the 1.5 ms synaptic delay; highlights last 3 ms for visibility. B: Pistons show full-population mean excitatory and inhibitory conductances onto E neurons and mean E/I voltages at the same timestep. Both conditions share conductance and voltage scales. C: Prescribed per-afferent rates, with a moving time cursor; E- and I-targeted envelopes coincide. The selector changes the recorded condition, while speed changes playback only. At 1×, one recorded second plays over 25 seconds. Positions and pulse appearance are display choices.</figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { mountCircuit } from './js/panel-a.js';
  class ThetaPingCircuit extends HTMLElement {
    dispose?: () => void;
    observer?: IntersectionObserver;
    revision = 0;
    onChange = () => { void this.load(); };
    async load() {
      const revision = ++this.revision;
      this.dispose?.(); this.dispose = undefined;
      const select = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-condition]')!;
      select.disabled = true;
      this.dataset.condition = select.value;
      const surface = this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.scene')!;
      surface.replaceChildren();
      const status = document.createElement('p');
      status.className = 'status'; status.setAttribute('role', 'status');
      status.textContent = 'Loading recorded circuit…'; surface.appendChild(status);
      this.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement | HTMLButtonElement>('[data-pause], [data-speed], [data-scrub]').forEach(control => { control.disabled = true; });
      this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-pause]')!.textContent = 'Pause';
      try {
        const dispose = await mountCircuit(this);
        if (this.isConnected && revision === this.revision) this.dispose = dispose;
        else dispose();
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Circuit replay could not start', error);
        status.textContent = 'Circuit replay is unavailable. Figure 3 shows both recorded rasters.';
      } finally { select.disabled = false; }
    }
    connectedCallback() {
      this.querySelector('[data-condition]')?.addEventListener('change', this.onChange);
      this.observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        if (!entries.some(entry => entry.isIntersecting)) return;
        this.observer?.disconnect(); void this.load();
      }, { rootMargin: '200px' });
      this.observer.observe(this);
    }
    disconnectedCallback() {
      this.revision++; this.observer?.disconnect(); this.dispose?.();
      this.querySelector('[data-condition]')?.removeEventListener('change', this.onChange);
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('theta-ping-circuit')) customElements.define('theta-ping-circuit', ThetaPingCircuit);
</script>

<style>
  theta-ping-circuit { display: block; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #d6dfe7; border-radius: 12px; background: white; }
  .scene { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 124 / 54; position: relative; }
  .scene :global(canvas) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .scene :global(.circuit-labels) { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .status { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-content: center; padding: 24px; margin: 0; text-align: center; }
  .controls { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; padding: 0 16px 8px; }
  select { font: inherit; color: #263343; background: white; border: 1px solid #cbd5df; border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px; }
  .controls label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font: 13px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; color: #263343; }
  input[type="range"] { width: 110px; accent-color: #626b74; }
  input.scrubber { flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 100px; width: auto; margin: 0; }
  .speed-control { flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .speed-control input { flex: 0 0 110px; }
  output { display: inline-block; width: 48px; min-width: 48px; flex: 0 0 48px; text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #176d91; outline-offset: 3px; }
  button { border: 1px solid #cbd5df; border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 14px; background: #f5f7f9; color: #263343; font: 13px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; min-width: 80px; }
  button:hover { background: #eaf0f4; }
  button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #176d91; outline-offset: 3px; }
  button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: default; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; }
  @media (min-width: 1180px) {
    figure { grid-column: text-start / page-end; display: grid; grid-template-columns: subgrid; }
    theta-ping-circuit { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    figcaption { grid-column: text; }
  }
</style>
